<%- include('_policy-head') %>
<section class="section"><div class="container-x max-w-3xl prose-ek">
  <h2>Minimum age</h2>
  <p>Puppies and kittens are handed over at a minimum of <strong>8 weeks</strong> of age, after weaning and their first vaccinations.</p>
  <h2>Health records</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every animal comes with its vaccination and deworming record. Microchip and registration (KCI) numbers are given where available.</li>
    <li>Imported animals are brought in with the import permit and health certificate required by the Department of Livestock Services. Listings show whether certificates are available.</li>
    <li>We keep a copy of these records for every animal sold.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Health check at handover</h2>
  <p>Each animal is examined before handover. We recommend a check up with your own vet within 7 days.</p>
  <h2>Health guarantee</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>If a vet diagnoses a serious infectious illness (such as parvovirus or distemper) within <strong>7 days</strong> of handover, we will treat the animal at our cost or offer a replacement.</li>
    <li>Congenital defects diagnosed by a registered vet within <strong>30 days</strong> are covered by a replacement or a refund, at your choice, on return of the animal.</li>
    <li>The guarantee does not cover illness caused by neglect, injury, or not following the vaccination schedule.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Reservations and returns</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A deposit reserves an animal for 72 hours. The balance is paid at handover.</li>
    <li>If you change your mind before handover, the deposit is refunded minus a 20% handling fee.</li>
    <li>Animals cannot be returned for a change of mind after handover, but please talk to us: we will always help rehome an animal rather than see it abandoned.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Welfare</h2>
  <p>We may refuse a sale if we believe the animal will not be properly cared for.</p>
</div></section>
